{"id": "clm:34cd47ee672b58d97dcb5ffb361d851522b5a11f671be9f9f034a0b3566d2204", "type": "statement", "text": "Applications do not need to precompute hashes to use a hashed index: MongoDB computes the hashes when resolving indexed queries. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:9dbf1dfb022c3e68eeaa7875b3889223cdac95195dfee429f4f78a8a2558b3c1", "type": "statement", "text": "Hashed indexes automatically compute hashes when resolving queries; applications do not need to precompute a $hash digest. Use $toHashedIndexKey for aggregation-side index-hash calculation, or convertShardKeyToHashed() in the shell. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toHashedIndexKey.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a02fbe552b7133af792fdbb4576ea80950b488911d7ed19e3197b7ec2119378a", "ev:a7f007bf13e5cc4a55b8bed14254092fc5bb6b070632e1b496dc9a28b2dd1f7c"]}
{"id": "clm:d1fcddc371ae20c706a10176eaeed24b6f75fad5b6bdea8db1a71254d8e2e5d6", "type": "statement", "text": "$hash returns null for null, undefined, or missing input. For other inputs, a value that is neither a valid UTF-8 string nor BinData produces an error. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3db042646b1e13b1b2621d9ae1bc4e453509ecf7a9a114f2ea0c0116479abed7"]}
{"id": "clm:d0bca401a412790211ba2c0cd44c290237e3ab290e29a5d34cfe0445b82e1b12", "type": "statement", "text": "An algorithm value outside the accepted set produces a $hash error. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:cd34f56c9d0d561a54fba19459ee9699d551e3c87d70e012f8b5145e5b66abca", "type": "statement", "text": "$hash raises an error for other input types or an unrecognized algorithm. A numeric or document value therefore needs an explicit application-defined representation before general-purpose hashing. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:69e804f80784533bbe410588af8bfe32fa20f3e2d188781dfc4b903d724a8646", "type": "statement", "text": "Percona lists $hash among the new expressions in its own Percona Server for MongoDB 8.3 Technical Preview announcement dated July 30, 2026. This supports distribution adoption, without independently verifying input/error behavior. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.percona.com/blog/percona-server-for-mongodb-8-3-technical-preview-is-now-available/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5d1f06564de8cddae713ce573e41922fa61a7441ca6150c90ef746888b204858", "ev:8d0aaae9e9c072b3ee17812902a7f84a15db1ed467dd4646ec740e72d31be401"]}
{"id": "clm:6432f811dfb2e4d66d50e470483510394db4176ec6a9987983da822f5c0b6dcf", "type": "statement", "text": "$toHashedIndexKey does not apply collation to strings, even under a non-simple aggregation collation. A hashed index can hash a collation key instead, so its hash can differ from the expression result for the same data. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toHashedIndexKey.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/SERVER-84462"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:27cb714f6305ef5d7ca2fc4a32d192c540208787b13e5f1ae9757052dc97956a", "ev:6b7b091c072c6e8ce793f94c22fc22b379b6e81ebb55acd9d60306f1d8469c16"]}
{"id": "clm:6943ca66191193caf499b9f6518769a67388172b6509a60ce0ea2538dc1eb3a6", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB documents $hash as new in 8.3; Percona also includes $hash among the aggregation expressions in its 8.3 technical preview. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-07-30)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/percona-server-for-mongodb-8-3-technical-preview-is-now-available/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:221b8a7312175883a1a0bb10067fe2c50d731ff3d6b35c4636f07892dab0b1ad", "ev:8d0aaae9e9c072b3ee17812902a7f84a15db1ed467dd4646ec740e72d31be401", "ev:edaf85dfc6040ee8b54d5464d0bfbe52e36fa4039a75230597ec569e4d7f1627"]}
{"id": "clm:e5262abd70842870015383165c2b924beccf8d18372c156665e8bae407b91942", "type": "statement", "text": "$hash computes a BinData digest from a valid UTF-8 string or BinData; $hexHash is the corresponding hexadecimal-string form. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/COMPASS-10200"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:221b8a7312175883a1a0bb10067fe2c50d731ff3d6b35c4636f07892dab0b1ad", "ev:aa346acc26fec9f5b3f56e69786c0fb0162adb7dc6decb01c5ec677d6ee9723d", "ev:acc7ef9dc56326ba6ad05e697c616d6fd6fd9858c82006cfca229c7eeefe594f"]}
{"id": "clm:6ef969ed2d07566eb612ab195e3b288bd50608184032e90f70c42f897846768a", "type": "statement", "text": "The syntax is { $hash: { input: <expression>, algorithm: <string> } }; both fields are required, and input must resolve to a valid UTF-8 string or BinData, apart from the documented nullish cases. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4b4f3677c116e75dc87097816d822e3dc7066038999ead3c18f8ad551646403a"]}
{"id": "clm:ee85438943673f265e3c49761b057df1970a75a2d593b7f49754554d59768bcf", "type": "statement", "text": "For null or a missing input field, $hash returns null; $toHashedIndexKey instead hashes null and missing values to a Long. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toHashedIndexKey.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:2f1edd8b64387aebd3f7dfe1c118c4e8984c6cf9d7f4a52eca39bf4e4f47e029", "type": "statement", "text": "$toHashedIndexKey uses MongoDB hashed-index hashing and returns a fixed-size numeric hash, whereas $hash is a general-purpose binary-digest expression. The operators serve different output and key semantics. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toHashedIndexKey.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:e33e5c088b10f7ddd4cfe173f45b6606361f125a8ec4a2ac7a5a6203d1f06855", "type": "statement", "text": "Hashed-index numeric semantics can collapse distinct inputs: the documented example gives 2.3, 2.2, and 2.9 the same hash after truncation to a 64-bit integer. An index hash is therefore unsuitable as a lossless identity for the original numeric value. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/indexes/index-types/index-hashed.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1deb6bb6eda501f36dcf702257b6a3e8567a2f0a8b1c3a56d2dfa3ecfdb89acf"]}
{"id": "clm:8c002d2eb07a9dc1173ec0ced4c7769a5397b3213f2fdbebd03d0c8efccff01d", "type": "statement", "text": "Migration Verifier documents that its toHashedIndexKey comparison mode can miss an equal-valued Long-to-Double type change. Hash-and-length comparison therefore does not establish full BSON binary equivalence. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb-labs/migration-verifier", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "NOT-SAMPLED", "evidence_ids": []}
{"id": "clm:6f34850c32221d71319dd5872c44d6efe5a05d4e1fe00b7e62a78c50b44ac80a", "type": "statement", "text": "NoSQLBooster 11.1 documents a $.hash({ input: \"$password\", algorithm: \"sha256\" }) operator helper for MongoDB 8.3 aggregation; its announcement says the helper includes inline code-completion documentation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-30)", "source_url": "https://nosqlbooster.com/blog/announcing-nosqlbooster-11-1/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3d72e8dafaed352d7c4192363e3efd39409b8fe0b90c3d7f80173d664e3c242c", "ev:9b8db8a9970616aee5634899734ffa02a191ce2d06f12a7b8624bd29d1cc2b11"]}
{"id": "clm:8aa028486f08d60173f362106005f8e202553d736943b80516eeca93dfc9e923", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB introduced $hash in 8.3 as an aggregation expression that returns a BinData digest from a UTF-8 string or binary input. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/8.3.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:221b8a7312175883a1a0bb10067fe2c50d731ff3d6b35c4636f07892dab0b1ad"]}
{"id": "clm:e97e984a74c61caf5fe7dac5e05bb0e40e06519a302213710e1c03bba9c28b95", "type": "statement", "text": "$hash returns null for null, undefined, or missing input. For null or missing values, $toHashedIndexKey instead returns a Long hash value; replacing one operator with the other changes null semantics. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/hash.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Aggregation binary hashing and hashed-index key separation"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/toHashedIndexKey.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5e8d3cbd303593a9c5d2f8847052d29468bed93db50f56d98b42bc17dcfeb866", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:2b38a2bb9ff0df7575d25525bdcab9e36fbcac5ee7313bbed1830b8e840bae51", "ev:d89ecf0ea0b726a0855357727ad351470d9df6ea83e1ba2842d4a6c0411f94db"]}
